WEBVTT

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:19.930
<pls: The Story of a Failure>
<pls: The Story of a Defector>
<eql: In

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:24.520
In other word

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:24.730
<pls: The Story of a Failure>
<pls: The Story of a Defector>
<eql: In other words, me.>

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:35.880
I'm sorry, Miach.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:46.120
It's been a while, tribe of medicine.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:49.460
Likewise, warriors of the Tuareg tribe.

00:02:57.130 --> 00:03:03.390
Do you know what "Tuareg" means in Arabic?

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.100
I'm afraid not.

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:08.180
It means "The people abandoned by God."

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:10.690
A terrible name given by outsiders.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:16.190
Being abandoned by God sounds fabulous to me.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.990
It sounds like you don't love your God.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:25.160
That's right. So we escape the eyes of God by being on the battlefield.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:33.920
This medical patch is also a product of that God.

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:47.970
I had thought that the Tuareg tribe rejected putting WatchMe in their bodies.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:52.270
We know to partake of it in moderation.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:59.570
We don't want to be controlled by your God who obtains data in the name of Lifeism.

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:05.910
As long as we update with physical media, we can deal even with new epidemics.

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:13.830
So this backroom deal is also a fine act of charity.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:19.260
You people don't know moderation.

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:26.050
You zealously impose your beliefs upon us,

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:29.560
not recognizing that doing so ignites conflict.

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:37.820
We are neither allies of the government of Niger nor of the Tuareg tribe.

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:43.990
As a cease-fire overseer, I am a rogue.

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:48.280
You of the medicine tribe, why don't you come with us?

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:51.330
We have a high regard for women.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:55.630
I'm grateful for the proposal, but I must decline.

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:01.760
I'm here because...

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:04.430
...I'm a coward.

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:20.190
I probably wasn't strong like her.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:24.820
I wasn't strong enough to go to the other side.

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:29.660
Tuan, are you willing to die with me?

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:35.290
I'm sorry, Miach.

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:40.630
A small aircraft from the Nigerien military is approaching!

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.720
It's a WarBird! It's armed!

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:48.340
Calm down! Fall back!

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:50.470
Let's hurry, Tuan!

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:52.810
You'll have trouble if the public finds out

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:56.390
a cease-fire inspector is doing backdoor booze deals

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:59.060
with a group she's supposed to be monitoring.

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:03.900
Farewell, medicine woman.
You're welcome to join us anytime.

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:05.780
Thanks.

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:19.040
It's no good, Tuan! They're catching up!

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:38.480
We're close enough to be captured on camera!

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:40.560
What are its communication capabilities?

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:45.150
They'll have gone radio silent until exiting the recon zone, in case of electronic attack.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:48.570
We'll take them down before the images are sent to headquarters!

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:50.450
Take the wheel!

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:52.910
We're gonna crash!

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:54.620
Shit!

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:03.500
I'll draw them in till we're just outside their range.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:06.590
Distance is 5700!

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:12.260
Distance is 3000!

00:07:12.470 --> 00:07:14.350
2500! 2000!

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:16.600
1500! Tuan!

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:24.570
Could you not interrupt my break on the battlefield?

00:07:56.510 --> 00:07:58.270
I'll leave the rest to you.

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:29.670
Thanks to my lofty job as "helix inspector,"

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:34.050
I left Japan and am wandering across the war zone.

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:42.440
I fled from a society that was like a prison.

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:47.190
From a society slowly strangling its people with kindness.

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:05.120
Tuan, are you willing to die with me?

00:09:10.340 --> 00:09:17.680
You're made of the same stuff as me, Tuan Kirie.

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:23.140
And from Miach Mihie...

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:15.780
Miach!

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:31.540
We'll show them together.

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:36.590
Together we'll make a proclamation to never become adults.

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:56.860
This body, these breasts, this secret place, this womb...

00:10:57.070 --> 00:11:03.950
We'll quietly cry out to the world that all of it is our own.

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:10.080
WatchMe is put in our bodies at birth,

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:13.540
and people not only aren't suspicious of it, they're actually thankful.

00:11:16.010 --> 00:11:19.340
WatchMe starts up on its own when we become adults

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:24.180
and takes away both our freedom to get fat and our freedom to die.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:31.770
Even the growth of your breasts is known and managed by the Admedistration.

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:34.820
Can you tolerate that?

00:11:38.150 --> 00:11:40.740
S-Stop it, Miach!

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:45.910
Can you stand the fact that your body continues to be supplanted

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:48.370
by the words and numbers of WatchMe?

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:52.120
I've had enough.

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:54.130
More than enough.

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:57.000
Miach!

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:05.070
Forgive Me, Miach

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:12.020
We're arriving at base, Tuan.

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:25.660
Helix inspectors. The Watchmen of Lifeism.

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:27.490
As the term "helix" suggests,

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:32.870
we monitor whether dangerous activities such as genetic manipulation are occurring.

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:36.460
The genetics version of the Worldwide Nuclear Institute.

00:12:36.670 --> 00:12:39.800
Before you knew it, our agency had expanded its scope,

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:42.590
assimilating divisions of the police and military,

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:50.430
and even intervening in conflicts under the lofty slogan of "preserving the right to live."

00:12:52.180 --> 00:12:53.730
Here you go.

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:56.310
Hey, treasure it.

00:12:56.520 --> 00:13:01.780
This battlefield is the only place
I've found to run away to.

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:08.700
I ran away slyly, secretly from the prison of compassion that strangles people.

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:14.710
I pretended to accept becoming an adult and tricked the system.

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:28.890
Tuan Kirie, Senior Inspector,
I've been waiting for you.

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:31.180
Chief Os Cara!

00:13:33.390 --> 00:13:36.190
What business do you have in my quarters?

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:41.030
I have an interest in whatever you just hid behind your back.

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:48.950
Bordeaux, eh? I hear it's heavy on Merlot,

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:54.370
and some years there are barrels that are 100% Merlot.

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:58.750
I may not look it, but I am 72.

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:02.300
I was the last generation to have the real experience of alcohol.

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:04.670
That's right.

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:10.050
The Nigerien cease-fire oversight team's position demands total impartiality.

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:13.850
Our helix inspector report will decide

00:14:14.060 --> 00:14:17.940
which cause receives support--
Niger or the Tuareg tribe.

00:14:18.150 --> 00:14:22.190
It would be a huge mess if the public knew we were making illegal deals with the Tuareg,

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:25.320
not to mention that we were up to our ears

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:29.240
in alcohol and tobacco, which are relics of the previous era.

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:32.870
How did you silence the WatchMe in your body in the first place?

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:35.750
The health management server's warning automatically--

00:14:35.960 --> 00:14:38.710
Women can use magic.

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:42.800
Although it seems you have forgotten that you're a woman, Chief.

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:46.050
I don't know what kind of dirty tricks you're using.

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:50.760
But because of you, overseeing this cease-fire will become very difficult.

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:52.930
That won't happen.

00:14:53.140 --> 00:14:56.810
This crest won't end up being tarnished.

00:14:57.020 --> 00:14:59.770
Because you won't make all that public.

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:02.400
My personal disgrace would be one thing,

00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:05.030
but if the office of helix inspector loses its authority,

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:09.320
the world's efforts toward peace and health will amount to nothing.

00:15:09.530 --> 00:15:12.870
That would be really unfortunate, Chief.

00:15:14.490 --> 00:15:19.160
Very well. However, you will accept your suspension!

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:25.000
Senior Inspector Tuan Kirie, until things calm down, you must return to the homeland!

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:26.260
The homeland...

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:28.590
Wait a minute. Are you joking?

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:32.300
I will not allow the battlefield to be used as a bar any longer.

00:15:32.510 --> 00:15:36.020
Thoroughly experience loving and being loved by your neighbors in Japan

00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:39.020
and relearn how to live in a community.

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:47.650
Dammit... Japan...

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:50.740
My teen-aged self abhorred it.

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:56.450
And Miach Mihie detested Japan with all her being.

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:01.670
I failed...

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:14.550
That I'm still alive means I failed...

00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:19.430
How powerless I was, and dependent on others...

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:21.520
If Miach Mihie were here,

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:26.570
if I had her guidance and the weapons she gave me, I would succeed.

00:16:26.770 --> 00:16:29.860
If I can't do it now, I'll never be able to accomplish anything,

00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:33.110
even if I go on dragging through life after this.

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:40.790
That's what I thought.
But that was such dependent thinking...

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:51.260
T-Tuan!

00:16:51.470 --> 00:16:53.050
I failed.

00:16:53.260 --> 00:16:55.510
Tuan! Are you there?

00:16:58.100 --> 00:17:02.310
Are you there? It's Mom! Are you there?

00:17:03.270 --> 00:17:06.770
I'm so glad... so glad, Tuan.

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:14.860
And Miach?

00:17:15.070 --> 00:17:17.120
Miach is...

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:26.790
I see... she's dead...

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:36.510
It's useless, Mother. It's completely useless.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:41.720
You can't go feeling guilty about every random person's death like that.

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:46.810
I mean, you didn't even have any contact with Miach.

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:49.360
Society makes us think we all care about each other;

00:17:49.570 --> 00:17:54.150
makes you nonsensically wonder why you couldn't stop the death

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:57.070
of someone you hardly knew.

00:17:57.280 --> 00:18:00.740
I'd had enough of that kind of world.

00:18:03.410 --> 00:18:10.840
Cian is all right. She's getting treatment at the Emergency Ethics Center.

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:16.590
I'm sorry, Miach.

00:18:23.520 --> 00:18:25.600
I will die.

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:41.450
What will the two of you do?

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:52.500
Miach was too smart, overly thorough, and always knew just how to go about things.

00:18:53.800 --> 00:18:57.930
Knew the single most masterful way to do them.

00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:07.730
Pills produced by MediCare.

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:14.690
Just by taking this, you can destroy all the nutrients in your body.

00:19:18.610 --> 00:19:20.530
I'll do it.

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:35.920
She was the charismatic leader for just the two of us, Cian and I.

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:40.680
An ideologue who knew far too many things and hated far too many things.

00:19:46.390 --> 00:19:49.100
I'm sorry, Miach.

00:20:03.530 --> 00:20:06.660
I'm not interested in normal people.

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:14.040
Miach Mihie was the problem child who had the best grades in the class.

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:17.090
She didn't fit into any group and kept to herself,

00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:20.510
in beautiful isolation in the classroom.

00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:26.310
She didn't try to talk to anyone other than me and Cian Reikado.

00:20:26.510 --> 00:20:32.020
When you want to be alone, it's best to rely on obsolete media.

00:20:32.230 --> 00:20:35.770
If you're looking for staying power, books are the strongest.

00:20:35.980 --> 00:20:37.940
Staying power?

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:40.490
Staying power in isolation.

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:43.860
It's just the two of us, me and the book.

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:50.040
Miach downloaded texts she wanted to read from the internet

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:54.330
and went so far as to get them bound by a bookbinder.

00:20:54.540 --> 00:20:58.460
While Miach swam in the great sea of words,

00:20:58.670 --> 00:21:04.090
she learned how to fashion herself into a societal weapon.

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:14.140
If we felt like it, in an instant we could annihilate everyone living in Japan.

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:24.660
Because all the adults have a magic box, you know.

00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:28.450
Ah... Miach!

00:21:31.370 --> 00:21:34.040
If you tampered with MediCare...

00:21:38.290 --> 00:21:42.210
Chemical weapons that would destroy this city...

00:21:44.090 --> 00:21:46.640
Medicine to make you feel good...

00:21:46.840 --> 00:21:49.600
All are things that you could synthesize.

00:21:49.810 --> 00:21:54.310
We're taught to believe that
MediCare can't do such things.

00:21:56.810 --> 00:22:00.190
But if we cheat the system...

00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:15.330
We can overthrow the world.

00:22:33.770 --> 00:22:41.400
The world becomes increasingly beautiful with health, wholesomeness, and peace.

00:22:41.610 --> 00:22:44.690
Those good intentions don't know when to stop.

00:22:46.240 --> 00:22:51.620
Japan, which I so violently detested and ran away from...

00:22:51.830 --> 00:22:54.370
--I have returned to it.
--Are you tired?

00:22:54.580 --> 00:22:59.370
The Haneda Airport has many kinds of health services available.

00:22:59.580 --> 00:23:02.000
Please take your time.

00:23:02.210 --> 00:23:05.760
Feel free to proceed to the nearest healthcare center.

00:23:06.880 --> 00:23:11.550
--Good afternoon and welcome to Japan, the country of hospitality.

00:23:09.130 --> 00:23:11.550
--It's the same.

00:23:11.760 --> 00:23:16.270
--A healthcare center is in every lounge.

00:23:11.760 --> 00:23:19.890
--Each person seeking comfort in doing the same thing as everyone else.

00:23:16.270 --> 00:23:23.610
--We advise MediCare access to everyone departing and returning.

00:23:25.440 --> 00:23:26.860
Thank you for your kindness.

00:23:26.860 --> 00:23:28.200
Thank you for your kindness.

00:23:28.400 --> 00:23:32.240
"All for one, and one for all."

00:23:32.450 --> 00:23:33.870
We are social resources.

00:23:32.450 --> 00:23:33.870
Warning: Low Blood Sugar

00:23:33.870 --> 00:23:36.080
We are social resources.

00:23:36.290 --> 00:23:41.830
--Have a healthy, happy, and caring day.

00:23:37.160 --> 00:23:41.830
--Tuan! Tuan! Tuan! Tuan! I found you!

00:23:42.040 --> 00:23:44.590
Long time no see, Cian.
You knew I'd be here?

00:23:44.800 --> 00:23:49.720
I was surprised! I got the news just yesterday that you'd be coming home.

00:23:49.930 --> 00:23:52.680
I was suddenly sent back.

00:23:52.890 --> 00:23:59.520
Cian Reikado. A good friend who tried to die with me thirteen years ago.

00:24:00.810 --> 00:24:05.270
Good afternoon and welcome to Japan, the country of hospitality.

00:24:05.480 --> 00:24:09.740
A healthcare center is in every lounge.

00:24:09.940 --> 00:24:17.910
--We advise MediCare access to everyone departing and returning.

00:24:12.410 --> 00:24:17.910
--Tuan, since helix inspectors stand out enough as it is, you should be a little careful.

00:24:18.120 --> 00:24:20.120
It's part of my job.

00:24:20.330 --> 00:24:25.790
Because war can take place in deserts or highlands or anywhere, I can't afford to care.

00:24:26.000 --> 00:24:32.180
Yeah! Your job is something important that contributes to society, isn't it?

00:24:33.890 --> 00:24:35.720
Will you visit your family today?

00:24:35.930 --> 00:24:38.970
I'll find a hotel.
There's no point in going home.

00:24:39.180 --> 00:24:40.640
No point?

00:24:40.850 --> 00:24:43.100
Everyone wants to hear what you have to say, you know.

00:24:43.310 --> 00:24:45.810
Who is "everyone"?

00:24:46.020 --> 00:24:51.280
Mom may want to gather the neighbors together and have a party, but that's boring.

00:24:46.060 --> 00:24:47.480
Safety

00:24:48.730 --> 00:24:50.530
Health

00:24:51.490 --> 00:24:51.740
Why?

00:24:51.740 --> 00:24:52.950
Society

00:24:52.950 --> 00:24:54.570
Because there's nothing to talk about.

00:24:52.950 --> 00:24:53.490
Society

00:24:54.780 --> 00:24:57.950
What about the Sahara?
And weren't you in Colombia before that?

00:24:58.160 --> 00:25:01.250
You're having really valuable experiences!

00:25:02.370 --> 00:25:05.460
You haven't changed a bit.

00:25:05.670 --> 00:25:09.380
No one wants to hear about the realities of a cruel battlefield.

00:25:09.590 --> 00:25:16.050
But you've finally come home, and I want the people here to know you.

00:25:16.260 --> 00:25:19.260
I don't want to know or be known by anyone.

00:25:19.470 --> 00:25:23.100
As for me, I'm not doing anything as great as your job,

00:25:23.310 --> 00:25:25.650
but I'm volunteering three days a week.

00:25:25.850 --> 00:25:29.270
Things like caring for the elderly and food distribution.

00:25:29.480 --> 00:25:34.530
I do online ethics sessions and health counseling about fifteen hours a month.

00:25:34.740 --> 00:25:36.240
I see.

00:25:36.450 --> 00:25:39.280
Would you like to come with me sometime?

00:25:42.250 --> 00:25:44.410
Okay, why don't we grab a bite to eat?

00:25:44.620 --> 00:25:47.290
There's a good restaurant near my place.

00:25:47.500 --> 00:25:48.540
The two of us?

00:25:48.750 --> 00:25:53.470
Yeah. And you could come to my place after if that's okay.

00:25:53.670 --> 00:25:58.470
My friend who tried to die with me so we could scar this world

00:25:58.680 --> 00:26:02.970
has settled completely into a typical, public-spirited lifestyle.

00:26:03.180 --> 00:26:06.350
Her WatchMe is tethered to the Admedistrative server.

00:26:06.560 --> 00:26:11.400
That's what it is to become an adult.

00:26:11.610 --> 00:26:14.650
The only one not getting with the program is me.

00:26:14.860 --> 00:26:18.110
I don't know whether that's pathetic or principled.

00:26:19.700 --> 00:26:21.990
Tuan! Are you okay?

00:26:22.200 --> 00:26:27.120
Are you feeling ill?
Would you like to sit down?

00:26:28.460 --> 00:26:30.340
--I'm fine!
--If I kept living in this country,

00:26:30.540 --> 00:26:33.550
--Tuan!
--I'd end up either killing myself or someone else.

00:26:33.760 --> 00:26:37.800
That's why I fled to the battlefield.

00:26:38.010 --> 00:26:41.430
The battlefield was crowded with all sorts of people.

00:26:41.640 --> 00:26:43.060
It's different here.

00:26:43.270 --> 00:26:47.190
Mostly everyone is the same here, as if we've wandered into a looking glass world.

00:26:47.390 --> 00:26:51.150
Don't you think you were rude to her?

00:26:51.360 --> 00:26:54.320
She's an important person on a council somewhere.

00:26:54.530 --> 00:26:59.030
--After Miach's death, Cian and I parted ways.

00:26:54.530 --> 00:26:56.700
--I know. Sorry.

00:26:59.240 --> 00:27:04.040
As if everything to that point was some ritual we all go through,

00:27:04.240 --> 00:27:07.460
Cian returned entirely to the straight and narrow.

00:27:07.660 --> 00:27:12.210
I pretended to do likewise, on the surface.

00:27:12.420 --> 00:27:15.760
I took Miach Mihie's place academically...

00:27:15.960 --> 00:27:22.050
...and I stored up the knowledge and hatred that she'd surely have gained if she'd lived.

00:27:35.860 --> 00:27:39.570
This brings back memories, right?
Eating lunch together.

00:27:39.780 --> 00:27:41.530
That's right.

00:27:44.180 --> 00:27:44.220
Please chew thoroughly.

00:27:50.960 --> 00:27:54.420
It's kind of weird. It being the two of us.

00:27:54.630 --> 00:27:58.420
There used to be three of us.

00:28:02.590 --> 00:28:08.270
Miach would always finish eating her bento first and then fold an airplane like that.

00:28:08.480 --> 00:28:10.230
Is that so?

00:28:13.100 --> 00:28:16.360
You grew your hair out.

00:28:16.570 --> 00:28:18.900
You look like Miach.

00:28:21.490 --> 00:28:26.200
You and Miach were friends before I joined you, right?

00:28:27.330 --> 00:28:30.290
I was captured against my will.

00:28:30.500 --> 00:28:32.420
Really?

00:28:32.620 --> 00:28:35.500
I didn't tell you that she waylaid me at a park on my way home

00:28:35.710 --> 00:28:40.010
and talked to me about books and solitude?

00:28:40.220 --> 00:28:45.050
I wonder if she was fishing for someone.

00:28:45.260 --> 00:28:48.520
Perhaps she was searching for a friend,

00:28:48.720 --> 00:28:50.850
someone who seemed likely to hang out with her.

00:28:51.060 --> 00:28:53.230
--Not really.
--What?

00:28:53.440 --> 00:28:58.530
Probably not. Not a friend.
Miach was looking for a comrade.

00:28:58.730 --> 00:29:00.900
Isn't that the same thing?

00:29:01.110 --> 00:29:04.280
No. Friends and comrades are different.

00:29:04.490 --> 00:29:07.410
They're both indisputably a type of companion, but...

00:29:07.620 --> 00:29:11.200
The bond between comrades is like the one between fellow soldiers.

00:29:11.410 --> 00:29:17.960
Maybe we weren't the sort of comrades Miach was hoping for, then...

00:29:18.960 --> 00:29:21.090
Probably not.

00:29:26.090 --> 00:29:32.140
Tuan, I have one thing I need to say.

00:29:32.350 --> 00:29:33.890
What?

00:29:34.100 --> 00:29:40.020
I didn't take the pills
I got from Miach that day.

00:29:40.230 --> 00:29:43.150
I betrayed you and snitched to my parents.

00:29:44.740 --> 00:29:46.570
Really?

00:29:46.780 --> 00:29:49.280
I was scared to take them.

00:29:50.410 --> 00:29:53.120
Tuan, aren't you mad?

00:29:53.330 --> 00:29:58.420
From where I'm sitting, I owe you my life.

00:29:58.630 --> 00:30:00.500
Thank you.

00:30:00.710 --> 00:30:03.050
But I'm still a traitor.

00:30:03.260 --> 00:30:06.260
It's my fault that Miach died.

00:30:06.470 --> 00:30:08.050
It's not your fault.

00:30:08.260 --> 00:30:10.760
No, it was my fault.

00:30:10.970 --> 00:30:13.180
I didn't have the courage to take the pills,

00:30:13.390 --> 00:30:15.600
and I didn't have the courage to immediately snitch,

00:30:15.810 --> 00:30:18.230
so when I shut myself off in my room without going to school,

00:30:18.440 --> 00:30:22.070
my mom took me to the Emergency Ethics Center.

00:30:22.280 --> 00:30:25.780
There, I spilled the beans about Miach's pills.

00:30:25.990 --> 00:30:31.330
The center immediately contacted your mom, and you pulled through.

00:30:31.530 --> 00:30:34.370
But... Miach...

00:30:34.580 --> 00:30:37.710
Miach's mother said that when their house was contacted

00:30:37.920 --> 00:30:45.130
she was already quite debilitated, and she didn't make it.

00:30:45.340 --> 00:30:49.640
I think you call it "being donated"?
Some organization got her body.

00:30:49.840 --> 00:30:54.060
Donated? I didn't know that...

00:30:54.270 --> 00:30:59.690
Maybe I wanted someone to tell me it wasn't my fault.

00:30:59.900 --> 00:31:04.150
The one time I visited
Miach's mother I heard about it.

00:31:04.360 --> 00:31:06.320
Should we stop talking about this?

00:31:06.530 --> 00:31:09.410
It's okay. Let me speak.

00:31:10.990 --> 00:31:12.490
Because when I think back on it now,

00:31:12.700 --> 00:31:19.080
I think my decision to be with Miach was because I thought she needed me.

00:31:19.290 --> 00:31:20.880
Needed?

00:31:21.080 --> 00:31:25.550
I think I fancied myself her "balancer."

00:31:25.760 --> 00:31:33.600
At the time, I felt like I had nowhere to belong, and I wanted to run away from the oppression.

00:31:33.810 --> 00:31:34.850
Yeah.

00:31:35.060 --> 00:31:41.150
But, I didn't want to die, or kill anyone!

00:31:41.350 --> 00:31:46.900
Miach was different and really lived on the edge.

00:31:47.110 --> 00:31:48.610
That's true.

00:31:48.820 --> 00:31:55.700
Yeah. I wanted to be by her side to help her hang on.

00:31:55.910 --> 00:32:02.290
I thought maybe agreeing with the things she said would make her feel better.

00:32:02.500 --> 00:32:10.220
But, ultimately I was just a coward and Miach died.

00:32:10.430 --> 00:32:14.350
It seems I didn't really know you.

00:32:14.550 --> 00:32:17.220
You're strong.

00:32:25.610 --> 00:32:27.650
Here you are.

00:32:35.330 --> 00:32:37.950
I'm sorry, Miach.

00:33:18.200 --> 00:33:26.170
Sorry... Miach... I'm sorry...

00:33:44.560 --> 00:33:46.940
What a shameful act!

00:33:47.150 --> 00:33:49.900
A blasphemy against Lifeism!

00:33:51.150 --> 00:33:56.700
The number of confirmed dead is currently 2,796.

00:33:56.910 --> 00:34:01.120
6,582 tried to commit suicide all at once on the same day and at the same time,

00:34:01.120 --> 00:34:06.250
Emergency Meeting Regarding the Worldwide

00:34:01.120 --> 00:34:06.250
Simultaneous Suicide Incident

00:34:02.330 --> 00:34:06.250
and of those, 2,796 were successful.

00:34:06.830 --> 00:34:11.840
Eight hours after the incident, some still hang between life and death,

00:34:12.050 --> 00:34:15.300
and it is thought that the number of deaths will increase.

00:34:18.850 --> 00:34:22.560
The method of suicide did not follow any pattern.

00:34:27.100 --> 00:34:32.320
Because about half of the suicides committed the act while wearing augmented contact lenses,

00:34:32.530 --> 00:34:35.780
their visual feeds can be viewed on the server.

00:35:10.440 --> 00:35:13.480
Please do not touch your Augmented Reality (AR)
Contact Lenses with soapy hands.

00:35:10.980 --> 00:35:13.690
Augmented Reality (AR)

00:35:10.980 --> 00:35:13.690
Contact Lenses Usage Warning

00:35:13.690 --> 00:35:15.730
Please remove your Augmented Reality (AR)
Contact Lenses before washing your face or the eye area.

00:35:14.320 --> 00:35:17.030
Augmented Reality (AR)

00:35:14.320 --> 00:35:17.030
Contact Lenses Usage Warning

00:35:23.950 --> 00:35:26.000
Your heart rate is increasing.

00:35:23.950 --> 00:35:26.000
Please calm down and

00:35:23.950 --> 00:35:26.000
get treatment for tachycardia.

00:35:35.340 --> 00:35:37.670
medical attention immediately.

00:35:35.340 --> 00:35:37.670
Please receive

00:35:42.470 --> 00:35:47.310
Is-Isn't this a terrorist attack on our Lifeist society?!

00:35:48.560 --> 00:35:50.770
What is the condition of the survivors?

00:35:50.980 --> 00:35:53.610
They've all fallen into a deep coma.

00:35:53.820 --> 00:35:59.610
Not a single survivor capable of answering questions about their motive has been found.

00:36:03.030 --> 00:36:05.030
The Helix Inspection Agency deems this incident

00:36:05.240 --> 00:36:09.660
a possible criminal act threatening the respect for Lifeism.

00:36:09.870 --> 00:36:12.460
We will investigate and resolve the matter at once.

00:36:12.670 --> 00:36:17.460
Two hours from now the WHO will hold an emergency meeting.

00:36:17.670 --> 00:36:21.050
Due to the treaty in effect between the Admedistration and the WHO,

00:36:21.260 --> 00:36:26.680
all helix inspectors will participate in each country's police investigations.

00:36:26.890 --> 00:36:30.140
Please take the initiative and make sure the whole world knows

00:36:30.350 --> 00:36:32.850
what helix inspectors are before we're through.

00:36:49.200 --> 00:36:51.250
Calling me on a secure line?

00:36:51.460 --> 00:36:53.460
Not only are you suspended,

00:36:53.670 --> 00:36:57.960
the victim Cian Reikado committed suicide right before your eyes.

00:36:58.170 --> 00:37:03.510
Take 120 hours of therapy with a psychological counselor and medication.

00:37:03.720 --> 00:37:06.300
You intend to leave me off this case.

00:37:06.510 --> 00:37:09.720
Esteemed Chief Inspector
Os Cara Stauffenberg.

00:37:09.930 --> 00:37:13.350
If you do that, I might just use my downtime to confess to the media

00:37:13.560 --> 00:37:19.360
what I was doing in Niger with the cease-fire team.

00:37:19.570 --> 00:37:21.070
Have you lost your mind?

00:37:21.280 --> 00:37:27.410
I am completely, without a doubt, full of spite and sane.

00:37:27.620 --> 00:37:30.750
Since helix inspectors often have assignments in conflict zones,

00:37:30.950 --> 00:37:37.000
they can get an exemption to prioritize the mission at hand over therapy.

00:37:37.210 --> 00:37:41.130
You're the one with the power to grant those exemptions.

00:37:44.340 --> 00:37:48.470
Very well. I will approve your participation in this matter.

00:37:48.680 --> 00:37:51.970
But you only have a grace period of five days.

00:37:52.180 --> 00:37:55.440
Even I can't extend it any longer.

00:38:01.110 --> 00:38:03.860
If I hadn't returned to Japan...

00:38:04.070 --> 00:38:06.070
If I hadn't reunited with Cian...

00:38:06.280 --> 00:38:09.200
Would she have ended up not dying?

00:38:14.120 --> 00:38:17.120
Miach had said...

00:38:17.330 --> 00:38:22.800
"It's easy for anyone to take a life, if they have a mind to.

00:38:23.010 --> 00:38:28.590
In fact, humans hold the power to destroy even more important things than life."

00:38:28.800 --> 00:38:31.560
She was just fifteen.

00:38:32.600 --> 00:38:39.440
Does this mean thirteen years later
Cian proved her right?

00:38:42.230 --> 00:38:46.030
I've been left behind once again.

00:38:47.530 --> 00:38:49.070
Five days.

00:38:49.280 --> 00:38:53.490
That's the time I've been given to solve Cian's death.

00:38:53.700 --> 00:38:57.580
It seems I didn't really know you.

00:38:57.790 --> 00:39:00.170
You're strong.

00:39:15.140 --> 00:39:17.810
I'm sorry, Miach.

00:39:44.750 --> 00:39:50.760
I'm sorry, Miach... I'm sorry.

00:40:00.810 --> 00:40:04.150
I'm sorry, Miach.

00:40:12.030 --> 00:40:14.990
One month after her death,
Miach Mihie's parents moved to

00:40:15.200 --> 00:40:18.250
the Fifth Tama District on the recommendation of the Admedistration.

00:40:18.450 --> 00:40:22.290
Request isolation mode with helix inspector privileges.

00:40:22.500 --> 00:40:26.300
Accepted. Senior Inspector Tuan Kirie's profile will not display for anyone

00:40:26.500 --> 00:40:29.420
with a social rating less than 5.

00:40:29.630 --> 00:40:31.840
The Mihie family's score is 3.

00:40:32.050 --> 00:40:34.760
Currently Reiko Mihie is home.

00:40:34.970 --> 00:40:39.980
Due to isolation mode, they will not be notified of Senior Inspector Tuan Kirie's visit.

00:40:53.660 --> 00:41:00.870
Back then we never cared about the existence of each other's parents,

00:41:01.080 --> 00:41:03.960
and never visited each other's houses.

00:41:20.560 --> 00:41:26.150
Since long ago, people have been tied down by various things.

00:41:26.360 --> 00:41:33.650
Families, companies, religion, money.

00:41:33.860 --> 00:41:37.030
Money was made of paper, you know.

00:41:37.240 --> 00:41:42.330
People always said, "A few scraps of paper can't make you happy,"

00:41:42.540 --> 00:41:45.830
but everyone was bound by money.

00:41:46.040 --> 00:41:53.010
War was waged over money, and girls sold their bodies for money.

00:41:54.930 --> 00:41:59.510
But you know, WatchMe is more problematic.

00:41:59.720 --> 00:42:07.560
It ties us down by taking something far more vital than money hostage.

00:42:12.360 --> 00:42:16.570
I wonder what kind of people
Miach's parents must be,

00:42:16.780 --> 00:42:24.120
to raise someone who'd say with a smile that she could kill thousands of people.

